%N A399286 Composite numbers whose number of digits and the number of digits in their largest prime factor are the same.
%C A399286 Terms > 9 are a subsequence of A084891. - _Michael S. Branicky_, Sep 07 2026
%H A399286 Michael S. Branicky, <a href="/A399286/b399286.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%e A399286 22 = 2*11 is a term since both it and 11 have two digits.
%e A399286 44 = 2^2*11 is a term since both it and 11 have two digits.
%e A399286 202 = 2*101 is a term since both it and 101 have three digits.
%t A399286 Select[Range[2, 382], !PrimeQ[#] && IntegerLength[#] == IntegerLength[Max[First /@ FactorInteger[#]]] &] (* _Stefano Spezia_, Sep 07 2026 *)
%o A399286 (Python)
%o A399286 from sympy import factorint
%o A399286 def ok(k): return k > 3 and k != (m:=max(factorint(k))) and len(str(k)) == len(str(m))
%o A399286 print([k for k in range(2, 385) if ok(k)]) # _Michael S. Branicky_, Sep 07 2026
